KG42.register("clusters-aa2df7291e8d4aead6577fca",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v142-d-K003","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","label":"Organization of regional trading and settlement-state selection after the cutoff","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Organization of regional trading and settlement-state selection after the cutoff","market_meaning":"The coordinator supervises local trading, organizes surplus and deficit trades between the region and the retailer, and bears responsibility for the billing mechanism. This paper retains P2P when the iteration limit is reached without convergence and settles using the final-round state; the exit arrangement in Ref. [17], which instead has each participant trade individually with the retailer, is retained as a separate conditional branch.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["coordination","pricing","activation","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Final-round P2P settlement in this paper and individual trading with the retailer in Ref. [17] are exit policies that must not be mixed. The requirement for local sharing before aggregated trading under a single PCC retains its network condition. The shared pricing and stopping chains provide interfaces only; this cluster does not claim that the final round has converged, is physically feasible, or has determined payment amounts for individual households.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"Trading organization, the cutoff trigger, adoption of the final-round state, and billing responsibility jointly constitute an identifiable procedural rule; price formation is primarily owned by K002, and actual billing formulas are outside the scope for which this cluster claims completeness.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries trading organization, the single-PCC condition, and two exit arrangements for nonconvergence with explicit source attribution."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Complements responsibility for the billing mechanism, the settlement cutoff, and the obligation in this paper to adopt the final-round state."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"References only the stopping conditions and the exit trigger in Ref. [17]; its price feedback and iterative process belong primarily to K002."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides the generation source for internal trading prices while P2P remains enabled; the pricing rules and unclosed boundaries still belong primarily to K002."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C007","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C008"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g07-ev-05"],"rationale":"Within the SDR scope where P2P is retained, the internal prices generated by the coordinator are used for local exchanges; this interface does not apply to the exit outcome in Ref. [17], which cancels P2P."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g03-E15"],"rationale":"Under the condition that the limit is reached without convergence, this paper specifies continued use of the final-round P2P result as the post-stopping trading arrangement; it does not interpret all stopping cases as nonconvergence."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-CN03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19"],"rationale":"The trigger of reaching the limit without convergence, explicitly attributed to Ref. [17], is paired with the outcome of cancelling P2P and trading individually with the retailer; it is not implemented simultaneously with this paper's policy."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-CN04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g03-E15"],"rationale":"Retaining the final-round P2P trading arrangement and settling according to the final-round state are the execution and settlement aspects of the same exit scheme in this paper; no new scientific causal edge is added."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-CN05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E15"],"rationale":"The source uses real-world trading deadlines to explain finite iteration and final settlement, supporting procedural coordination between the stopping process and settlement timing, but provides no numerical conversion from iteration count to actual time."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-CN06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05"],"rationale":"The source assigns trading supervision and operation of the billing mechanism to the coordinator, respectively complementing execution and settlement responsibilities; the two duties and their corresponding edges are not duplicate objects."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-OM01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R010::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05"],"rationale":"The same ESR coordinator is responsible for trading supervision and the billing mechanism; display through a representative does not merge execution edges with payment edges."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-OM02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g07-ev-05"],"rationale":"Within this cluster's SDR scope where P2P is retained, the internal-pricing function is the same in generation, coordination, and use for local trading; this interface is not carried over when the exit outcome is individual trading with the retailer."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"Trading responsibility, exit policies, and settlement-state selection all depend on candidate evidence that has not been independently reviewed; assembled indicates only that the described procedural candidate can be assembled.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g07-ev-05"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the attribution of the policies to this paper and Ref. [17], the single-PCC condition, and the source text on final-round settlement, keeping the two exit branches separate."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G02","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The existing chains lack details on household-level bills, the handling of metering deviations, and the pairing of final-round bids with price snapshots, and provide no conversion between real-world deadlines and the iteration limit. Procedural state selection does not fill these gaps in executable settlement details.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::param_max_iterations","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g03-E15"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If expanded into executable payment rules, obtain or clarify the missing provisions for metering, snapshots, timing, and cash flows; billing formulas must not be automatically inferred from internal prices or final-round wording."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Dedicated nodes for the retailer, external reference prices, exit, and settlement at the cutoff remain proposals pending review; existing references do not mean that they have been approved, nor do they treat the retailer as the coordinator or a local prosumer.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006","v141-c-R008::theta::theta-r-retail","v141-c-R008::theta::theta-r-export","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g03-E15"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-prop01","v141-b-g02-prop02","v141-b-g02-prop06","v141-b-g03-P02"],"required_work":"Manually examine the ontological boundaries of external counterparties, price inputs, and exit procedures; handle these upstream if subsequent expansion is approved. Only references to frozen objects are retained in this round."}]},"rule_refs":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R005","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R010","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R004","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","COMP-315d42da2c8d28d8","COMP-6ea6fa7e2454dda5","KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","KG31-8571e493b8ecf84a","KG31-a9bd9e360b96ff06","KG31-e3df7b859b17cba0"]});
